{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lnzkh9aG47wqynFfjBkR2g","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_7/projects/gen-depth-contamination/writing_plan.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"meta:\\\\n  venue: EMNLP 2026 Main\\\\n  track: ARR May 2026\\\\n  template: null\\\\n  template_note: \\\\\\\"ARR uses ACL Rolling Review format (acl2023.sty). Will use standard ACL LaTeX class from EMNLP 2025 call.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  page_limit: 8\\\\n  deadline: 2026-05-25\\\\n  core_claim: >\\\\n    K*=2 is the generational discrimination boundary for 1.5B-scale models under standard nucleus decoding.\\\\n    Depth features are 70-85% text-intrinsic (Pythia↔OLMo 91% transfer retention).\\\\n    Even coarse 3-class ordinal signal enables graduated filtering that outperforms binary approaches.\\\\n  created_at: 2026-05-13T12:00:00Z\\\\n  partial_draft: true\\\\n  partial_scope: [method, experiments_c1, related_work, introduction]\\\\n  deferred_sections: [abstract, experiments_c3, conclusion]\\\\n  deferred_reason: \\\\\\\"exp-006 (graduated filtering) and exp-003 (decoding ablation) not yet complete\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\npaper_outline:\\\\n  - section: abstract\\\\n    word_budget: 250\\\\n    status: deferred\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Problem: Web data contaminated by multi-generational recursive synthetic text; binary detectors ignore depth\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Method: Formalize as iterated lossy channel; DPI guarantees finite K*; 15D feature pipeline + OBD-LightGBM\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"C1': K*=2 across 4 model configs (bootstrap 95% CI), 70-85% text-intrinsic signal\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"C3: [TODO exp-006] Graduated filtering outperforms binary on MMLU/HellaSwag\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments_c1, experiments_c3, method]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: introduction\\\\n    word_budget: 1200\\\\n    status: writable\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Hook: First-gen synthetic text retains ~85% information structure of source; fourth-gen is qualitatively different — yet binary detectors treat them identically\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Gap: Binary detection doesn't estimate depth; model collapse literature describes macro phenomenon without detection tools; data selection methods ignore recursive depth\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Insight: Recursive generation = iterated lossy channel; DPI guarantees finite K*; we are first to systematically measure it\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Mechanism: 15D statistical feature pipeline + ordinal classifier; K* operationalized via θ=0.60 AUC threshold with bootstrap CI\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Contributions: C1' (K* characterization: K*=2 across 4 models, cross-model transfer 70-85% text-intrinsic, degradation ordering ρ≥0.85, generation mode analysis) + C3 (graduated filtering, pending exp-006)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments_c1]\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"shumailov2024collapse (model collapse seminal)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"drayson2025 (closest prior work)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"basani2026diveye, zhang2024minkpp (binary detection)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"schaeffer2025position (collapse taxonomy)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    figures: [fig1_pipeline]\\\\n    registry_refs: [exp_007_bootstrap_ci]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: related_work\\\\n    word_budget: 800\\\\n    status: writable\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Model Collapse & Recursive Generation: Shumailov 2024 (Nature, seminal), Alemohammad 2024 (self-consuming MAD), Dohmatob 2024 (scaling law perspective), Schaeffer 2025 (8 definitions taxonomy — K* = Family B D4+D6), Kazdan 2025 (accumulate vs replace), Shi 2025 (memorization transition) → macro phenomenon, no per-text detection tool\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Binary Synthetic Text Detection: Zellers 2019 (Grover), Ippolito 2020, DivEye (Basani 2026), Min-K%++ (Zhang 2024), CoDeC (Zawalski 2026) → binary boundary only, AUC_{1v2} ≤ 0.53 for depth\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Data Selection & Curation: DSIR (Xie 2023), D4 (Tirumala 2023), DoReMi (Xie 2023) → distribution matching without depth; Drayson 2025 = closest (binary MGT + SIR for collapse prevention, our ordinal generalization); Amin 2025 (weak signal suffices); Gambetta 2025 (surplexity)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Watermarking & Provenance: Kirchenbauer 2023 → complementary when watermarks available; our method works on unwatermarked text\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [introduction]\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Position Drayson 2025 as closest prior work: SIR is special case of graduated filtering when K*=1\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Adopt Schaeffer 2025 taxonomy explicitly: K* = distributions deforming (Family B)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: method\\\\n    word_budget: 1500\\\\n    status: writable\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.1 Problem Formulation: Recursive generation as iterated lossy channel X → Y₁ → Y₂ → ...; DPI: I(X;Y_k) monotonically decreasing → convergence guaranteed → finite K*_theory exists\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.2 Feature Extraction: 15D statistical features in 5 groups (surprisal moments, surprisal derivatives, frequency diversity, tail-thinning, self-similarity); computed via external scorer model on tokenized text\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.3 Ordinal Binary Decomposition Classifier: OBD-LightGBM — K binary classifiers for K+1 depth levels; ordinal structure enforced by cumulative probability decomposition; advantage over multiclass (exp-010: lower MAE)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.4 K* Operationalization: K*_empirical = max k s.t. AUC(k,k+1) bootstrap 95% CI lower > θ; θ=0.60 as operational threshold (justified by permutation test null distribution); K*_empirical ≤ K*_theory (conservative lower bound)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.5 Experimental Setup: 3 model families (Pythia-1.4B, OLMo-1B, Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct) × 2 generation modes; C4 seed corpus (5K docs); nucleus sampling p=0.95 T=1.0; depth 0-5; 5-fold stratified CV\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.6 Generation Mode Control: continuation (complete truncated prefix) vs rewrite (instruction-based rewrite); continuation as canonical condition for cross-model claims; rewrite as upper bound with mode-specific confound\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    notation_table:\\\\n      X: \\\\\\\"original human-written text\\\\\\\"\\\\n      Y_k: \\\\\\\"k-th generation synthetic text\\\\\\\"\\\\n      G_delta: \\\\\\\"LLM generation function with decoding strategy δ\\\\\\\"\\\\n      K_star: \\\\\\\"generational discrimination boundary\\\\\\\"\\\\n      theta: \\\\\\\"operational AUC threshold (0.60)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      f: \\\\\\\"15D feature extraction function\\\\\\\"\\\\n    tables: [tab_features, tab_setup]\\\\n    figures: [fig1_pipeline]\\\\n    registry_refs: [exp_010_ordinal_baseline]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: experiments_c1\\\\n    word_budget: 1800\\\\n    status: writable\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.1 K*=2 Across All Configurations: 4-model bootstrap CI table; all 1v2 CI_lower > 0.60; all 2v3 CI_upper < 0.60; permutation p < 0.002 for all 1v2; most marginal = Qwen-cont (CI_lower=0.6015); sharp AUC drop from 0v1 (~0.995) to 1v2 (~0.61-0.70) to 2v3 (~0.55-0.59)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.2 Cross-Model Transfer: 4×4 accuracy matrix + retention analysis; Pythia↔OLMo 91-92% retention → depth signal 70-85% text-intrinsic; 0v1 AUC >0.96 universally; Qwen-rewrite catastrophic transfer (61-63%); Qwen-cont much better (80-85%); confirms continuation as canonical\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.3 Feature Degradation Ordering: Spearman ρ ≥ 0.85 on single-feature AUC ranking (continuation, Pythia vs OLMo = 0.95); shared top features: surp_d1_std, surp_std, surp_d2_std; limitation: depth-pair level τ~0.37 at 1v2\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.4 Generation Mode Effect: rewrite AUC 1v2=0.6957 vs continuation 0.6114 (Δ=+8.4pp); transfer asymmetry cont→rw 89% > rw→cont 82%; rewrite amplifies depth signal via instruction-following artifacts but reduces cross-model generalizability\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    tables: [tab_kstar_ci, tab_transfer_matrix, tab_top_features]\\\\n    figures: [fig2_auc_decay, fig3_transfer_heatmap]\\\\n    registry_refs:\\\\n      - exp_001_pythia_depth\\\\n      - exp_002_olmo_depth\\\\n      - exp_017_qwen_continuation\\\\n      - mvp_pilot_sat_v1\\\\n      - exp_007_bootstrap_ci\\\\n      - exp_013_cross_transfer\\\\n      - exp_005_degradation\\\\n\\\\n  - section: experiments_c3\\\\n    word_budget: 1000\\\\n    status: deferred\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"[TODO exp-006] 6 filtering strategies × 5 seeds × α sweep\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"[TODO exp-006] Graduated vs binary on MMLU/HellaSwag\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"[TODO exp-006] α sensitivity + DSIR baseline comparison\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments_c1]\\\\n    tables: [tab_filtering]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: conclusion\\\\n    word_budget: 400\\\\n    status: deferred\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Summary: K*=2 first systematic measurement + cross-model transferability + graduated filtering\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Limitations: 1.5B-scale only; C4 English only; prompt-chain not retrain-chain; K* = operational lower bound\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Future: retrain-chain validation; larger models; multilingual; temporal dynamics of web contamination\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments_c1, experiments_c3, method]\\\\n\\\\nvisualization_plan:\\\\n  - fig_id: fig1_pipeline\\\\n    type: conceptual\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"System overview diagram: recursive generation chain (X → Y₁ → Y₂ → ... → Y_K) → 15D feature extraction → OBD-LightGBM depth classifier → K* determination via bootstrap CI. Clean academic style with arrows and labeled components.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: method\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"16:6\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"manual (conceptual diagram)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig2_auc_decay\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"Pairwise AUC decay curves across depth pairs (0v1, 1v2, 2v3, 3v4, 4v5) for 4 model configurations. Horizontal dashed line at θ=0.60. Error bars from bootstrap 95% CI. X-axis: depth pair, Y-axis: AUC. Shows K*=2 boundary clearly — all curves cross θ between 1v2 and 2v3.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments_c1\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"4:3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp_007_bootstrap_ci\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig3_transfer_heatmap\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"4×4 cross-model transfer accuracy heatmap. Rows = training source (Qwen-rw, Pythia, OLMo, Qwen-cont), columns = evaluation target. Annotated with accuracy values. Color scale from low (Qwen-rw cross-transfer ~0.26) to high (diagonal ~0.38-0.42). Highlight Pythia↔OLMo cluster.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments_c1\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"1:1\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp_013_cross_transfer\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig4_filtering\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    status: deferred\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"[DEFERRED] Graduated vs binary filtering comparison on MMLU/HellaSwag.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments_c3\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"[TODO exp-006]\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\ntable_plan:\\\\n  - table_id: tab_kstar_ci\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Pairwise depth discrimination AUC with bootstrap 95\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\% CI across four model configurations. All 1v2 CI lower bounds exceed $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\theta=0.60$; all 2v3 CI upper bounds fall below $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\theta$, establishing $K^*=2$.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments_c1\\\\n    type: statistics\\\\n    columns: [Configuration, Generation Mode, \\\\\\\"AUC$_{0v1}$\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"AUC$_{1v2}$\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"95\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\% CI$_{1v2}$\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"$p_{1v2}$\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"AUC$_{2v3}$\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"95\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\% CI$_{2v3}$\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp_007_bootstrap_ci\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"Bold 1v2 values above threshold. Report permutation test p-values.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_transfer_matrix\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Cross-model transfer accuracy matrix (6-class ordinal depth classification). Diagonal entries show within-model performance; off-diagonal entries show cross-model transfer.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments_c1\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [\\\\\\\"Train $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\backslash$ Test\\\\\\\", Qwen-rw, Pythia, OLMo, Qwen-cont]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp_013_cross_transfer\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"Report retention percentage (off-diagonal / diagonal). Highlight Pythia↔OLMo 91-92% and Qwen-rw 61-63%.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_top_features\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Top-3 discriminative features by single-feature AUC ranking across model configurations (continuation mode only). Spearman $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\rho$ between model pairs shown below.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments_c1\\\\n    type: statistics\\\\n    columns: [Rank, Pythia-1.4B, OLMo-1B, Qwen-1.5B-cont]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp_005_degradation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"surp_d1_std, surp_std, surp_d2_std shared across all architectures.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_features\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"15-dimensional feature set for depth estimation, organized by feature group.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: method\\\\n    type: configuration\\\\n    columns: [Group, Feature, Description]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_setup\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Experimental configurations for recursive depth chain generation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: method\\\\n    type: configuration\\\\n    columns: [ID, Model, Parameters, Generation Mode, N, Max Depth]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"manual + registry specs\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_filtering\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"[DEFERRED] Downstream evaluation: filtering strategy comparison.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments_c3\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    status: deferred\\\\n    columns: [Strategy, MMLU, HellaSwag, \\\\\\\"Δ vs no-filter\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"[TODO exp-006]\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nliterature_strategy:\\\\n  citation_budget: 30\\\\n  macro_context:\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"recursive synthetic text contamination and generational depth\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"data curation and quality estimation for LLM pretraining\\\\\\\"\\\\n  micro_clusters:\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"model-collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"model collapse iterative training synthetic data 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"recursive generation quality degradation LLM\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - shumailov2024collapse\\\\n        - alemohammad2024selfconsuming\\\\n        - dohmatob2024model\\\\n        - schaeffer2025position\\\\n        - kazdan2025collapse\\\\n        - shi2025generalization\\\\n      target_count: 6\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"detection\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"machine generated text detection statistical 2024 2025 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"AI text detection zero-shot features\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - basani2026diveye\\\\n        - zhang2024minkpp\\\\n        - zellers2019grover\\\\n        - ippolito2020detection\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"verification-curation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"data selection pretraining LLM synthetic filtering 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"synthetic data curation importance resampling\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - drayson2025\\\\n        - xie2023dsir\\\\n        - tirumala2024d4\\\\n        - xie2024doremi\\\\n        - amin2025escaping\\\\n        - gambetta2025surplexity\\\\n      target_count: 7\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"watermarking\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"LLM watermarking provenance tracking 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - kirchenbauer2023watermark\\\\n      target_count: 2\\\\n\\\\nwriting_order:\\\\n  - method\\\\n  - experiments_c1\\\\n  - related_work\\\\n  - introduction\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 13727, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011r7KfwDvszPyToacDstDaB","session_id":"d036397e-ac85-42a6-8c08-46d9d21a8d2f","uuid":"057d27ae-abcb-47ca-8b9d-117ec266a8bf","timestamp":"2026-05-13T09:01:56.747Z"}
